      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "First, you must understand that a VPN connection timeout occurs when your remote device cannot successfully establish a secure tunnel to the OmniCorp server, often due to network congestion, firewall blocks, or incorrect authentication credentials. Before attempting any technical fixes, please verify that your internet connection is stable by testing other websites or streaming services on the same device to rule out local bandwidth issues. Next, ensure that your VPN client application is fully updated to the latest version available on the OmniCorp support portal, as outdated software frequently causes handshake failures with modern encryption protocols. If the issue persists, try restarting your router and modem to clear any temporary routing tables that might be interfering with the specific IP addresses required for secure access. Additionally, check your firewall settings to confirm that the necessary ports for OmniCorp's VPN protocol are not being blocked by third-party security software or corporate network policies. You may also need to manually select a different server location from the dropdown menu if your current geographic node is experiencing high latency or maintenance downtime. Finally, if none of these steps resolve the timeout, please contact your local IT support desk with your employee ID and the specific error code displayed in the status window.",
